Q=[
make(1,"Listen to the exchange: 'The movie starts at 6:40.' 'Then let's meet outside the theater at 6:20.' When will they meet?",{"A":"6:20","B":"6:40","C":"7:00","D":"5:40"},"A","The second speaker directly says they will meet at 6:20; 6:40 is the movie start time, not the meeting time.","Separate the event time from the earlier meeting time and match the question to the correct one.",["Identify the event: the movie starts at 6:40.","Listen for the proposed meeting time.","Notice outside the theater at 6:20.","Distinguish meeting from movie-start time.","Choose A because it answers when they meet."],"easy"),
make(2,"Listen: 'Why are you carrying an umbrella?' 'The forecast says rain this afternoon.' Why is the person carrying it?",{"A":"Because rain is expected","B":"Because the umbrella is a gift for a birthday","C":"Because the bus is late","D":"Because the afternoon class moved"},"A","The forecast predicts rain, which is the explicit reason for carrying an umbrella.","Use the answer to the why question as the stated cause, not an unrelated detail.",["Identify the action: carrying an umbrella.","Find the reason introduced by the forecast.","Connect a rain forecast with an umbrella.","Reject birthday, bus, and class explanations because they are absent.","Select A and restate the cause in your own words."],"easy"),
make(3,"Listen: 'Where should I leave these science boxes?' 'Put them beside the cabinet near the back door.' Where should the boxes go?",{"A":"Beside the cabinet near the back door","B":"On the playground","C":"Inside the teacher's bag","D":"Under the front desk"},"A","The speaker gives a precise location: beside the cabinet near the back door.","Hold the location phrase as a complete unit and ignore places not mentioned.",["Identify the object being moved: science boxes.","Listen for the location command Put them.","Keep both landmarks: cabinet and back door.","Eliminate playground, bag, and front desk.","Choose A because it repeats the full location accurately."],"easy"),
make(4,"Listen: 'How many tickets do we need?' 'Three—one for Dad, one for Mom, and one for me.' How many tickets are needed?",{"A":"Two","B":"Three","C":"Four","D":"Five"},"B","The speaker lists tickets for three people, so three tickets are needed.","Count the explicitly named people rather than guessing from the family context.",["Find the question asking for a number.","Count Dad as one ticket.","Count Mom and the speaker as two more.","Compare the total with the choices.","Choose B because one plus one plus one equals three."],"easy"),
make(5,"Listen: 'I practiced the song all week, but I forgot the first line on stage.' How does the speaker probably feel?",{"A":"Disappointed but still prepared","B":"Completely unaware of the song","C":"Angry about the weather","D":"Certain the concert was canceled"},"A","Practicing shows preparation, while forgetting the first line suggests disappointment; the dialogue supports both parts of A.","Combine the effort clue with the mistake clue to infer a mixed feeling.",["Notice the speaker practiced all week.","Notice the contrast word but.","Identify the problem: forgetting the first line.","Combine preparation with disappointment.","Choose A because it includes both supported feelings."],"medium"),
make(6,"Listen: 'First wash the apples. Next, cut them into small pieces.' What should the listener do first?",{"A":"Wash the apples","B":"Cut the apples","C":"Bake the apples","D":"Put them in a bag"},"A","The sequence marker First introduces washing before the later cutting step.","Follow sequence words such as first and next before selecting an action.",["Find the first sequence marker.","Match First with wash the apples.","Keep cut for the second step introduced by Next.","Reject baking and bagging because they are not stated.","Select A and preserve the order of the instructions."],"easy"),
make(7,"Listen: 'I wanted to ride my bike, but the tire is flat. I'll take the bus instead.' What will the speaker do?",{"A":"Take the bus","B":"Repair the tire immediately","C":"Ride the bike anyway","D":"Stay at home all day"},"A","The flat tire prevents the planned bike ride, and the speaker explicitly chooses the bus instead.","Use the contrast and the final decision, which normally carries the next action.",["Identify the original plan: ride a bike.","Find the problem: the tire is flat.","Listen for the replacement signaled by instead.","Match the replacement action with take the bus.","Choose A because it is the stated next action."],"medium"),
make(8,"Listen: 'The green backpack is lighter than the black one, but the black one has more pockets.' Which statement is correct?",{"A":"The green bag is lighter, and the black bag has more pockets","B":"Both bags have the same weight and pockets","C":"The black bag is lighter and has fewer pockets","D":"The green bag has more pockets and is heavier"},"A","The comparison gives two facts: green is lighter; black has more pockets.","Track each comparative phrase separately and combine the two results.",["Record the weight comparison: green is lighter.","Record the pocket comparison: black has more.","Keep both facts instead of letting one replace the other.","Reject choices that reverse either comparison.","Choose A because it preserves both clauses."],"medium"),
make(9,"Listen: 'Could you email the homework tonight?' 'I can, after I finish dinner.' What does the second speaker mean?",{"A":"The email will be sent after dinner","B":"The homework has already been deleted","C":"Dinner is canceled","D":"The speaker refuses to help"},"A","I can accepts the request, and after I finish dinner gives the condition and timing for sending the email.","Interpret the modal response together with the time clause rather than treating after as refusal.",["Identify the request: email the homework tonight.","Notice I can as acceptance.","Read the time condition after dinner.","Connect the accepted action with its later timing.","Select A because it states the complete meaning."],"medium"),
make(10,"Listen: 'The community garden needs water, so our class will visit it on Saturday morning.' What is the main idea?",{"A":"The class plans a Saturday visit to water a garden","B":"The class is selling flowers on Friday","C":"The garden is closed for the whole month","D":"The students are taking a test Saturday morning"},"A","The need for water explains the class's plan to visit the community garden on Saturday morning.","Combine the cause and planned action to form a complete main-idea summary.",["Identify the problem: the garden needs water.","Find the response: the class will visit it.","Keep the time detail Saturday morning.","Reject activities and dates not stated in the recording.","Choose A because it summarizes the reason, action, place, and time."],"hard"),
]
